> This is not a bug, but correct (and very nice) behaviour. It works like 
> this: when naming, you can name a class of objects ('call') or a single 
> object ('name'). When you call something, every similar object that you 
> find will automatically also be called that. When you name something, 
> only objects that stack with it will get that name.
> 
> For example, if you deduce from the price in a shop what scroll is ID, 
> you /call/ it 'id'. This way, if you later find the same scroll, it will 
> also be called 'id'. However, if you have an elven dagger that your pet 
> won't step on, you /name/ it 'cursed'. Only other daggers that stack 
> with it (same enchantment and buc status) will also be named 'cursed' 
> (and stack with the other one).
> 
